LegaCore CONSTRAINT DERIVATION revision 3, frozen BEFORE the surgical pair that tests it.

WHAT CHANGED: nothing about which constraints are derived. Revision 3 reproduces revision 2 exactly
on all three existing families - requirements, generalization and provenance, identical counts. What
it adds is the ACCOUNT:

    requirement_resolution.resolved     [{ symbol, provider: existing_definition | planned_operation }]
    requirement_resolution.unresolved   [{ symbol, reason }]
    constraint_status.requirement_complete

WHY: h07 derived the correct region while silently dropping `math`, because a co-occurring resolvable
requirement already implied the same ordering. Behavioural success concealed an incomplete proof, and
nothing in the output could say so. Constraint sufficiency and requirement completeness are separate
properties.

WITNESSED: completeness.test.mjs shows h07 at region 5/5 with requirement_complete=false and
unresolved ["math"], against h08 - the same program apart from how its provider arrives - at
complete=true. The difference is attributable to exactly one thing.

STANDING: development. h07 diagnosed the gap this revision reports. The surgical pair authored after
this freeze is what would make the unresolved path prospectively tested, and it must be built so the
unresolved requirement is the ONLY mechanism capable of producing the expected narrowing.

